<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="69521" href="schedule/2019/spring/CS/598/69521.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2019" href="schedule/2019.xml">2019</calendarYear><term id="120191" href="schedule/2019/spring.xml">Spring 2019</term><subject id="CS" href="schedule/2019/spring/CS.xml">Computer Science</subject><course id="598" href="schedule/2019/spring/CS/598.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>TXU</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Reliable Software Systems</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course teaches the principles and practices of building reliable software systems. We will look into how software systems fail in the real world, study practical, widely-adtoped reliability techniques and practices, and discuss the state-of-the-art research of software and system reliability. This is a research-oriented seminar course with a major course project. Prerequisite:  CS 241 (System Programming) or CS 423 (Operating Systems Design)</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2019-01-14Z</startDate><endDate>2019-05-01Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="S3 ">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>03:30 PM</start><end>04:45 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>1304</roomNumber><buildingName>Siebel Center for Comp Sci</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Xu" firstName="T">Xu, T</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>